; Tutorial_9_Conclusion.inix -- what to carry away, the words HomerView uses, and where to learn more.

[about]
Title=9 - Conclusion
Intro=The conclusion and summary of the walks; the words HomerView uses, in two voices; then more information: the help built in and where to learn more.
Setup=Nothing is needed; this walk is listened to.
Homework=Open a page you read often and use three HomerView commands on it.

[step]

Say=To finish: what to carry away, the words HomerView uses, and where to get help. First, the summary. HomerView does only what your screen reader cannot, so the two together cover a page: your reader for headings and links, HomerView for what lies behind them.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus L, Link Target

[step]

Say=Every command is in one list, so nothing has to be remembered first.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F10, the command list

[step]

Say=And it works in its own window, so it never gets in your reader's way elsewhere.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Control plus Shift plus H

[step]

Say=Now the words, in alphabetical order. I say the term; the reader says what it means.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=axe-core.
Key=
Hear=Deque's accessibility engine, run by Alt plus Shift plus A.

[step]

Say=Copy Append.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus C: the selection, or the line, added to what is already on the clipboard.

[step]

Say=Equal Access.
Key=
Hear=IBM's accessibility engine, run by Alt plus Shift plus E, with Section 508 and EN 301 549 folded in.

[step]

Say=Extract Main Content.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F9: the article alone, in a tab of its own.

[step]

Say=Link Target.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus L: what is at the other end of a link, before you go.

[step]

Say=pattern.
Key=
Hear=A regular expression: a description of text to find, such as any four digits.

[step]

Say=Probable Main.
Key=
Hear=Where the page's content most likely begins, declared or weighed.

[step]

Say=profile.
Key=
Hear=HomerView's own browser settings and sign-ins, kept apart from your ordinary browsing.

[step]

Say=Read All.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F8: the whole page from the top, without moving the cursor.

[step]

Say=Web Download.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus W: every document on a page, fetched with the browser's own sign-in.

[step]

Say=Last, more information. Every command, by name, and every key with the version.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F10
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus H

[step]

Say=HomerView dot m d is the guide, with its own tutorial and troubleshooting; hotkeys dot m d lists every key; and the HomerView page on GitHub, at github dot com slash JamalMazrui slash HomerView, has the newest version.
Key=
Hear=
